  "workload_sha256": "31c599caa7344c938b588a0f22404cfcfe5fe53b3ef5fae40a568130cfadfca4",
  "D045_text": "| D045 | Freeze the falsifiable Architecture-B hypothesis: under W08, B's median-of-five M2 read-admission P99 must improve by at least 20% from A's 21-cycle baseline (at most 16 cycles); M1 aggregate read+write payload throughput may regress by no more than 5%; neither M0 direction's admission P99 may regress by more than 10%. W12 Jain grant-rate index must remain >=0.98 and starvation must remain bounded under documented recurring-service assumptions. Also report area and the same five-seed routed timing sweep. | FROZEN before B RTL | BENCH/HYPOTHESIS. W08 A results show 21-cycle M2 read admission P99, but 65-cycle response P99 and 86-cycle end-to-end P99 are also affected by the depth-8 FIFO endpoint. QoS is hypothesized to improve admission; response-tail improvement is not assumed. See `results/processed/arch_a_measurement/summary.md`. |",
  "D045_sha256": "700eb342707d4e153a2dccaf512b9e9c737735323a38ba88067e43690cd3b276",
  "D047_text": "| D047 | Reject Architecture B under the frozen D045 criteria; retain the measured B implementation as a functional experimental variant without post-result tuning. | FROZEN after Mission 4 comparison | BENCH/DECISION. Full matched five-seed W00\u2013W13 runs pass, and B meets W08 M2 read P99, W08 M0 read P99 and W12 Jain criteria. B fails the W08 M1 throughput floor (6.340714 vs 10.076650 bytes/cycle minimum; 59.78% of A) and W08 M0 write admission P99 (69 vs 29-cycle maximum). Matched ECP5 wrapper routes show 55 MHz all-seed timing-clean for B vs 60 MHz for A and higher resource counts. See `results/processed/ab_comparison/summary.md`. Any future scheduler change is a new experiment and cannot revise these results. |",
  "D047_sha256": "5c55452a9d9e505534d132695ee72e0500ec4b141d67946c6b7e4cf75ac694a6",
